## Provider routing (peak OpenRouter requests)

Injected on every OpenRouter-bound chat/completions call (including the
compressor when it peak-reroutes to an OR twin). Default **sort stays
`throughput`**; latency cap + ignore list push slow hosts to the back without
switching the sort key.

| Knob | Env | Default | Effect |
| ---- | --- | ------- | ------ |
| Sticky session | (gateway session id) | process `sess_*` | Body `session_id` + header `X-Session-Id` from turn 1 so OpenRouter reuses the same host (warm KV cache). Sessions expire after ~10 min idle on OpenRouter's side. |
| `provider.sort` | `DISCURSIVE_OPENROUTER_SORT` | `throughput` | Existing sort hint. Unset defaults to throughput; `none` / `off` / empty omits sort. |
| `provider.preferred_max_latency` | `DISCURSIVE_OPENROUTER_MAX_LATENCY_P90` | `2.5` (seconds, p90) | Soft preference — 15s hosts fall back in ranking. `0` or `off` omits the field. |
| `provider.ignore` | `DISCURSIVE_OPENROUTER_IGNORE` | `wafer,morph,venice` | Skip known-slow / flaky GLM Flash hosts. `none` / `off` / empty env value disables. |

`gateway_request` logs `latency_ms` and `or_host` (from `X-OpenRouter-Provider`
when present, else SSE/`openrouter_metadata` selected provider). Requests also
send `X-OpenRouter-Metadata: enabled` so the JSON/SSE path can name the host
when the header is absent.

### `OpenRouter host lottery / 15–60s GLM Flash turns`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| Peak GLM Flash / DeepSeek turns hit 15–60s TTFB; next turn may be fast or equally slow; cache hits do not stick | OpenRouter load-balances across hosts (Wafer ~15s p50) unless `session_id` is set from turn 1; `sort: throughput` alone does not exclude slow endpoints | Keep default throughput sort; send sticky `session_id`; set `preferred_max_latency.p90`; ignore `wafer,morph,venice`; confirm `or_host` on `gateway_request` |

## Credits endpoint

`GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/credits` returns `data.total_credits` and `data.total_usage`. Remaining credits = `total_credits - total_usage`. The balance is returned as USD (not a credit count). The endpoint may require a management key; on 401/403 surface an error string in the UI tooltip.

